"ph", "country_name": "Philippines", "summary": "Folk music can have a number of different meanings, including:\n\nTraditional music: The original meaning of the term \"folk music\" was synonymous with the term \"Traditional music\", also often including Roots music; the term \"Traditional music\" was given its more specific meaning to distinguish it from the other definitions that \"Folk music\" is now considered to encompass.\nFolk music can also describe a particular kind of popular music which is based on traditional music.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Olivia Rodrigo", "streams": 697192, "best_position": 17}, {"artist": "Ben&Ben", "streams": 428681, "best_position": 34}, {"artist": "Ellie Goulding", "streams": 206915, "best_position": 61}, {"artist": "Bleachers", "streams": 176384, "best_position": 92}, {"artist": "Clairo", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Ed Sheeran", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Faye Webster", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Jeff Buckley", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Lizzy McAlpine", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Mac DeMarco", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "One Direction", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Phoebe Bridgers", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "funk": {"genre": "funk", "country_code": "ph", "country_name": "Philippines", "summary": "Funk is an American music genre that originated in the late 1960s when African American musicians blended soul music, soul jazz and R&B into a rhythmic, danceable new form of music. Funk de-emphasizes melody and harmony and brings a strong rhythmic groove of electric bass and drums to the foreground. Funk songs are often based on an extended vamp on a single chord, distinguishing it from R&B and soul songs centered around chord progressions.\nLike much African-inspired music.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Bruno Mars", "streams": 718024, "best_position": 16}, {"artist": "Earl Agustin", "streams": 423862, "best_position": 50}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Harry Styles", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "IV Of Spades", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Omar Apollo", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "hip-hop": {"genre": "hip-hop", "country_code": "ph", "country_name": "Philippines", "summary": "Hip-Hop, also spelled Hip Hop or HipHop is a rhythm focused popular music style, originating from New York in The 70s. The term rap is sometimes used synonymously with Hip-Hop music. Hip-hop arose when DJs began isolating the percussion break from funk or disco songs for audiences to dance to.\nIt is now seen as a worldwide and popular genre ranging from American Mainstream (e.g. Eminem, Lil Wayne) to British Underground (e.g. Wiley, EMC Junkie ect).", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Mac Miller", "streams": 282470, "best_position": 21}, {"artist": "Miguel", "streams": 193139, "best_position": 71}, {"artist": "Justin Bieber", "streams": 183300, "best_position": 83}, {"artist": "Hev Abi", "streams": 171003, "best_position": 97}, {"artist": "Al James", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Chris Brown", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Doja Cat", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Drake", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Frank Ocean", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Joji", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "KATSEYE", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "jazz": {"genre": "jazz", "country_code": "ph", "country_name": "Philippines", "summary": "Jazz is a musical art form which originated around the beginning of the 20th century in Black communities in the Southern United States from a confluence of African and European music traditions. The style's West African pedigree is evident in its use of blue notes, call-and-response, improvisation, polyrhythms, syncopation, and the swung note of ragtime.\n\nFrom its early development until the present, jazz has also incorporated music from 19th and 20th century American popular music, which is based on European music traditions.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Up Dharma Down", "streams": 453528, "best_position": 43}, {"artist": "Lady Gaga", "streams": 172052, "best_position": 96}, {"artist": "Kendrick Lamar", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Laufey", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Lauv", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Rex Orange County", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Steve Lacy", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "k-pop": {"genre": "k-pop", "country_code": "ph", "country_name": "Philippines", "summary": "K-pop means Korean pop, which is\u00a0a musical genre, sometimes described more as an umbrella term, consisting of different music styles, including hip-hop, rap, jazz, r&b, dance, rock music and ballads. The name for the genre is first recorded in English around 1990\u201395. Strongly influenced by Western popular music, K-pop took off in 1992 with Seo Taiji and Boys, who incorporated rap, rock, and dance elements into Korean popular music.\nModern\u00a0K-pop \"idol\" culture\u00a0began later in the 1990s, as K-pop idol music grew into a\u00a0subculture.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "KATSEYE", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "LE SSERAFIM", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "NewJeans", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "pop": {"genre": "pop", "country_code": "ph", "country_name": "Philippines", "summary": "Pop music is a broad-term for many different types of music: The term is flexible, and the music labeled \"pop\" changes frequently. It usually refers to popular, appealing and mostly mainstream music with emphasis on catchy melodies and an accessible style, with songs that tend to have a short to medium length. Some subgenres may include synthpop, electropop, bubblegum, sophisti-pop, hyperpop and many others.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Arthur Nery", "streams": 762600, "best_position": 20}, {"artist": "Bruno Mars", "streams": 718024, "best_position": 16}, {"artist": "AD\u00c9LA", "streams": 715001, "best_position": 4}, {"artist": "Olivia Rodrigo", "streams": 697192, "best_position": 17}, {"artist": "Katy Perry", "streams": 531061, "best_position": 19}, {"artist": "Adie", "streams": 511835, "best_position": 13}, {"artist": "Ben&Ben", "streams": 428681, "best_position": 34}, {"artist": "December Avenue", "streams": 423841, "best_position": 41}, {"artist": "The Script", "streams": 297322, "best_position": 18}, {"artist": "Malcolm Todd", "streams": 279798, "best_position": 23}, {"artist": "Ariana Grande", "streams": 218425, "best_position": 51}, {"artist": "Yeng Constantino", "streams": 211196, "best_position": 57}]}, "r&b": {"genre": "r&b", "country_code": "ph", "country_name": "Philippines", "summary": "R&B is a musical genre that began to develop as a distinct style in the early 1950s. Originally known as rhythm and blues, it was primarily created by African American musicians and drew influence from both blues and early rock 'n' roll, with significant interaction between these genres. Over time, musicians from different backgrounds adopted the style and introduced new elements. In the 1950s, artists like Muddy Waters contributed to shaping the genre by emphasizing faster melodies and energetic rhythms.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Arthur Nery", "streams": 762600, "best_position": 20}, {"artist": "Bruno Mars", "streams": 718024, "best_position": 16}, {"artist": "Daniel Caesar", "streams": 376509, "best_position": 60}, {"artist": "Malcolm Todd", "streams": 279798, "best_position": 23}, {"artist": "Ariana Grande", "stream